{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792523414,"nonce":"jM64nUh4coEfzTl3qiJcKjvb2Lg=","message":"Fixed recursive ExprTools.map/iter traversal of grouped local declarations. Reproducer: recursively map `macro { var a = 1, b = 2; return a + b; }`. Haxe visits eight nodes; the previous Rayzor release recursed until stopped. Converting an ExprDef EVars record through the parser AST wrapped it in a block, revisiting the same grouped declaration. Traverse raw ExprDef records directly, preserve their position, and keep native expression inputs in native form for build-field consumers.\n\nCoverage: compiler unit test exercises both map and iter, grouped declaration shape and position; LSP initialization-macro fixture now has grouped locals before inline markup and checks the transformed function body in expansion preview as well as completion. Combined compiler/LSP tests: 773 compiler + 6 LSP unit + 13 LSP sessions pass. Real sibling RayDE session passes hover/completion/outline. The optimized release LSP probe, with RAYZOR_STD_PATH unset and the installed Haxe stdlib, reports zero recursion-limit and zero macro-budget errors. The debug test still encounters budget errors and is not representative of release macro execution speed.\n\nFull Mac arm64 conformance rerun: 1092 PASS / 148 SKIP, identical rows/outcomes to the previous clean run. Fresh release binary and source hashes recorded and unchanged during the run. cargo fmt --all -- --check, git diff --check and cargo clippy --workspace --all-features --all-targets -- -D warnings pass.\n\nRemaining RayDE release errors: IconSet.build reported undefined, CssCompiler undefined inside useUserAgent, haxe.io type lookup in Welcome, and initialization Extensions undefined. Important diagnostic follow-up: execute_build_macro maps every nested UndefinedVariable into UndefinedMacro for the outer call, potentially hiding the real IconSet failure. CssCompiler exists in the same package but only in #if macro; inspect the macro dependency graph. RayDE build.hxml omits the backend/library class paths present in scripts/deps.sh; its saved Haxe diagnostics also fail with Type not found: Extension. Do not hardcode those paths into the compiler.\n\nArtifacts: /tmp/rayzor-lsp-recursive-map/{verified-tests.log,rayde.log,release-rayde.log,release-rayde-stderr.log,conformance/report.tsv,environment.json,clippy.log}. Macro project support remains open.","files":null}]}